WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.730
Let's play the Yamanote Line game!

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.480
Things that are cute!

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:07.940
Rabbits.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.400
Little blonde girls.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.020
Um, kittens.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.740
Puppies.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.990
Uh, um... Shino!

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:19.990
Alice.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.270
Shino.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.320
Alice.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.120
Shino.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:24.920
Alice.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.580
Shino.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.210
Alice.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:26.750
Shino.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:27.380
Alice.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:27.880
Shino.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:28.290
Alice.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:28.630
Shino.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.210
Alice.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.100
Shino!

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.010
They're so clingy!

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.720
It's so hot.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.160
You said it.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.740
Summer vacation starts next week.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.240
I hope we can all go somewhere together.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.670
I know! I know!

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.620
Let's go to the beach!

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.880
What?

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.120
But I prefer the mountains.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.820
Yamanote Line game!

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.920
Places we want to go in summer!

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.420
The beach!

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:30.880
The mountains!

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:31.380
The beach!

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:31.880
The mountains!

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.500
Mountains!

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.500
You're so stubborn!

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.210
Stop fighting, you two.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.090
Why don't we compromise and do something at home?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.850
How is that a compromise?!

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:45.560
I don't mind where we go, as long as it's cool.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.850
We'll have fun anywhere, as long as we're together.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.270
What?

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.850
Come on! Let's go to the beach.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:51.860
I don't want to.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.030
I'll burn.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.070
You'd look good in a swimsuit. You're lucky.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.860
What are you talking about?

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.570
Just so you know, I'm an average size.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.120
If that's average, then that makes me...

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.540
Why do you have to be so difficult?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.290
I went to a beach recently.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.330
In Hawaii!

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.580
Blue skies, white clouds...

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.590
Sounds like fun!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.480
I spent a weekend there.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.220
But I'm taller...

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.810
Don't worry about that.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.390
Just stick some pads in and everything will be okay.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.400
Come on, let's have a snappy comeback.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.730
Why did you bring that to school?

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.030
We can't come to an agreement.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.240
What were we talking about?

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.950
How about this?

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.240
Let's play cards and the winner can choose what we do.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.410
Bring it on!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.420
The mountains... I wanted to go to the mountains...

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.960
Oh, fine.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.170
We'll go to the mountains, then.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.380
Mount Fuji!

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.880
I don't know about that...

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.640
It's so hot.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.890
Did you forget anything?

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:10.640
Nope.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.730
Water bottle, rain gear, bug spray.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.690
I left my swimsuit at home.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:17.860
Very good.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.940
Thanks for waiting.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.910
Shino, aren't you hot?

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.370
That's not the right outfit for the mountains.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.910
Is it some kind of cosplay?

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.860
I'm a forest fairy.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.300
What are you talking about?

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.590
Are you okay?

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.130
I'm a forest girl.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.420
Why not a mountain girl?

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.470
Because forest girls are cuter.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.290
Shino, you're so cute.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.300
You look just like a fairy.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.960
Really?

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.480
I don't want to see a fairy in so much pain.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:59.570
A girl doesn't mind enduring a little hardship to look good.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.360
That's what my sister told me.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.860
So hot...

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.990
Fine, but try not to collapse.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.450
Okay.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.620
Karen sure is late, though, isn't she?

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.910
She should be coming with her father.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:13.750
There they are.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.340
What is this?

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.330
Hi!

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.090
Get in, everyone!

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.090
Who <i>are</i> you?!

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.600
She must be rich.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.400
<i>It's summer vacation.</i>

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.400
<i>We're not going to Mount Fuji, but we're still going climbing.</i>

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.830
The mountains!

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.840
Woohoo!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.170
It's so hot.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.960
I feel like I'm gonna sweat my sunscreen off.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.800
Are you out of breath?

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.760
People blow on their food like this...

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.850
...when they eat hot stew, right?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.010
I see.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.350
You're cooling down the air.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.480
What are you two doing?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.530
You're all so slow.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.240
Are we nearly there?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.780
I bet it'll feel like an accomplishment when we reach the top.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:33.910
You're right.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.360
Let's do this.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.370
Hey, not that way.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.680
Hey, everyone.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.090
We can do some stream fishing here!

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.180
All the fishing equipment has been set up...

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.350
...by my father.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.730
This is what you were really after?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.300
Leave the fishing to me.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.700
When I lived in England, I could really show 'em at fishing.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.030
"Show 'em"?

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.240
I'll catch us a fish for lunch.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.660
I'll try to catch a big one.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.960
<i>I need to show Shino how great I am.</i>

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.250
<i>I can't let Karen beat me.</i>

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.250
Alice, you're burning...

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.380
All right.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.510
I caught another one.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.680
This one's a big one!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.510
You're amazing, Karen.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.570
I've been good at fishing ever since I was little.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:43.980
Alice?

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.440
Just you wait, Shino!

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.110
I'll catch you a tasty fish right now!

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.240
It's fine, really!

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.490
I appreciate the thought!

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.490
Let's eat!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.460
It's good, isn't it, Alice?

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.120
Yeah.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.630
Oh, that reminds me...

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.830
I made lunch for everyone.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.240
If you'd like...

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.800
Hooray.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.900
What?

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.010
I've got a little better.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.520
It looks delicious.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.510
You're right.

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:25.100
It's really good.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.110
I wish you were my you-know-what.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.530
Your what?

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.110
You know, my mum.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.990
This tastes just like my mum's cooking.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.870
There are lots of bugs out here.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:45.960
You're right.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.750
Shino, watch out!

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.260
Alice?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:56.760
I-I'm sorry, there was a mosquito... a mosquito...

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:57.970
Aya!

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.680
Please.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:05.140
I feel like I can do anything when I'm with you.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.670
What?

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.150
Where did that come from?

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.320
Let's dive from there!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.190
No chance!

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:18.620
I should've brought my swimsuit.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.590
You want to swim that badly?

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.420
We'll have to make do with just playing in the water.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.920
That's what us young people should do!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.000
All right.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.130
It's so cold.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.560
Come on, Aya.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:37.960
The water's nice.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:40.140
Now you've done it!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.560
You're wide open.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.100
Why, you...

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.350
There!

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.940
<i>Just for a little bit.</i>

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.070
Shino, I found a crab.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.850
Wow, a crab?

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:57.950
I want to see.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:01.780
Shino!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.080
Here I go!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.630
You're in for it now!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:11.170
How's this?

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.840
That's against the rules.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.140
Aya, hurry up!

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:24.010
Just... wait there...

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.310
Shino!

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:34.360
Shino!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:39.530
All the water it soaked up made it really heavy.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.320
Shino, are you hurt?

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.750
Geez...

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.500
Sorry, everyone.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.920
Well, it's summer. We'll dry out quickly.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.510
But my clothes will still be dirty.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.650
It's your fault for wearing that outfit.

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:06.010
You're still a fairy even without that outfit, Shino.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:07.730
It's all right.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.520
<i>We caught lots of fish in the stream.</i>

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:17.530
<i>Shino told me that the fish I cooked for her tasted good.</i>

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.900
<i>I'd like to try climbing Mount Fuji someday.</i>

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.370
How nice.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.040
How long have you been there, Shino?!

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.110
Alice!

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:34.920
Karen!

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.570
What am I going to do?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.420
They...

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:53.230
Did you drop the Golden Alice or the Golden Karen?

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:56.840
No, I could never choose!

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.480
Never!

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:00.990
What the heck?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:14.790
Blondes...

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:18.020
Shino, you really like blonde hair, don't you?

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:19.500
How about this one?

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:24.010
There are all kinds of hair colours there!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.350
Blue hair might be nice, too.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.240
No!

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.520
Don't dye your hair weird colours!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.190
You're so cute, Alice.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:46.430
It's a hand-me-down, but there!

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:47.200
All done.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.970
Thank you, Shino.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.450
Did you bring one too, Karen?

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:52.960
Yes.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.920
I've never been to a Japanese festival before.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:01.590
Me neither.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:04.800
Everyone helps haul a float with a big samurai on it, right?

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:05.960
A float?

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:07.070
Like a root beer float?

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.640
That's an Aomori festival.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.350
The festival we're going to today is the local summer festival.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.230
What?

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.340
There won't be any bonfires or shrines?

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.190
I don't believe so.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.400
I see.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.890
Alice, hold this.

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:24.400
What?

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.070
How nice.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.780
Oh, my!

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:30.780
What?

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.760
Blonde hair and a yukata.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:34.830
It's a good combination.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.790
Shino, what are you going to wear?

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.790
I'm wearing...

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.680
Thanks for waiting.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.990
Youko.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.230
What?

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.190
You look good in a yukata.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.690
Maybe it's because you have black hair.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.250
Y-You look-

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:06.190
Thanks for waiting.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.200
That's unconventional.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.950
Lanterns, torii gates, happi coats!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.210
Happy?

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:19.710
You wear them when you're happy.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:21.880
You're lying again.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.710
Onii-chan!

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.010
Karasuma-sensei.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.140
Oh, hello, girls.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.800
Karasu-chan, are you lost?

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.000
Did you get separated from your brother?

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.260
What?

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:40.150
No, I came by myself.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.650
But you've got three.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:45.690
I... well...

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:49.030
I'm going to eat them all myself!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.160
You'll get fat.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:56.870
What should we eat first?

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:57.910
Maybe something starchy?

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.290
Fried food is good, too.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.250
Cotton candy is for dessert.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.420
Chocolate bananas are dessert, too.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.900
I don't know what to get.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.720
Let's start by walking around and seeing what we want to eat and do.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:11.930
What?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.800
I want to eat now.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:22.070
But as soon as you get full, you'll find something you
really want to eat, and you won't have the money left.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:22.940
That happens a lot.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.320
Oh, well, that's...

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.530
We have to think before we eat.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:30.950
The takoyaki's really good.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.070
You're already eating.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:32.910
No fair.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.640
Hey, boss!

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:36.280
One takoyaki, please!

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:37.500
Yes, ma'am.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:41.420
Oh, um... Three hundred yen.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.040
Oh, three hundred yen?

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.670
Are you going to get any, Alice?

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:46.750
I'm fine.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.210
Would you like one?

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.190
Really?

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:50.170
Thank you.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.680
They're hot, so be careful.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.680
Why didn't you tell me that first?!

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.270
Now that that's over with, let's go.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.190
Go, go!

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.660
I want this.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.870
Karen, I think you should look in a mirror.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.410
You too, Alice.

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:24.920
They're so excited.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:28.630
The battle's on!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:29.750
Bring it!

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.920
You're quite good at this, aren't you?

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.180
This ought to work!

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.390
Bye-bye.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.350
But we went through all that trouble to catch them.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.980
It's catch and release.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:55.700
I almost had it...

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.470
I did it.

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:59.350
I'm done, too.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:01.160
What is that?

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.660
It's the Eiffel Tower.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.660
I lost.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:09.540
How unfortunate.

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:13.910
What is that?

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.510
Is it a fire?

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.390
The sound of a festival!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:24.060
Oh, I hope they let us join in.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.020
Hey, Karen!

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.810
Oh well.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.570
Youko, why don't you go, too?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:31.730
What about you?

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.570
I'll watch from here.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.430
What?

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.080
Aya, are you-

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.250
Youko!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:44.120
Ayaya!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:48.880
I thought only the drummers were allowed up there.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.000
They do whatever they please.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.490
How does the dance go?

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:56.180
I believe it's like...

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:01.010
That's it.

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:07.170
What's up?!

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:08.650
Yeah!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.290
That was fun.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.290
All that's left are the fireworks.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.370
When will they launch the fireworks?

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.540
Boom!

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.420
Unfortunately...

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.840
There isn't a fireworks display.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:35.500
What?

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:36.970
No fireworks at all?

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.930
Fireworks!

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.800
I have some.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.350
You have fireworks?

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.770
Yes.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.810
They can't compare to skyrockets, though.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.650
Yay!

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:53.820
Don't swing that around!

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.070
They're beautiful.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:57.820
Yeah.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.320
Aya.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.580
Where have you been?

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.120
Aren't you going to light a sparkler?

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.120
Here.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:13.130
How long has it been hurting?

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:15.960
Since we were standing at the station.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:17.460
From the very beginning?

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.380
Why didn't you say something?

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:22.470
I didn't want to put a damper on our festival experience.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:29.230
It stings because you let it go for so long.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.060
Say something next time.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.610
I know!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:35.480
Sparklers, huh?

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.400
That's nice.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:38.280
Isa-nee.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.280
Do you want to light a sparkler?

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.990
I'm fine.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.240
Isami, what did you buy?

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.290
A watermelon.

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.660
A watermelon!

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.670
We just went to the festival together.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.750
These are for you.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.420
I don't think I can eat all of that by myself.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:04.590
Shino.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:08.060
Thank you for taking me to the festival.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.100
How was it?

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:12.560
It was a ton of fun.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:15.980
It's the most fun I've ever had, too.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.180
Really?

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.360
Was this festival better than others?

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:23.740
Well, it may have been because I was with you.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:24.990
Shino.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.990
It's burned out.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.790
Summer's going to end.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.000
There are still plenty of fireworks.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.010
Yeah.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.300
You do have skyrockets!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.530
Don't.

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:50.060
You have to launch those in a wide open space.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:53.730
You already lit it?!

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.100
Don't point it this way!

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.530
Evacuate!

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.400
What am I supposed to do?

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:03.650
Douse it in water!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.860
Stay away!

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.990
No!

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:49.800
The girl sat all alone, facing her desk all night.

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:54.810
In that quiet room... tick tock, tick tock, tick tock.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:58.520
Only the sound of the clock echoed through the room.

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:02.540
Tick tock, tick tock, tick tock.

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:06.610
At midnight on the 1st of September,

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:10.990
she hadn't completed a single summer assignment!

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:14.990
Don't act like that doesn't describe you.

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:17.000
It's already 31st August.

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:23.260
I'll try writing a haiku about my memories of summer.

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:26.610
My very first time, mountains and a festival, me and Shinobu.

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:29.900
With the fireworks, Karen was so dangerous, me and Shinobu.

00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:33.180
You don't have to force my name into each one...

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:34.010
See you.

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:35.000
Good night.
